  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RECOVERING OF TIGERS THROUGH SMART PATROL, CONSERVATION EDUCATION, AND LONG-TERM POPULATION MONITORING IN THE WESTERN FOREST COMPLEX, THAILAND: SAVING THE TIGERS YEAR 13-15</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO: (1) STRENGTHEN THE SPATIAL MONITORING AND REPORTING TOOL (SMART) PATROL SYSTEM IN THUNG YAI WEST WILDLIFE SANCTUARY (TYW) THROUGH TRAINING, MORALE BOOSTING SUPPORT, AND MONITORING PERFORMANCE (2) STRENGTHEN THE CONSERVATION EDUCATION IN LOCAL SCHOOLS (3) MONITOR TIGERS AND THEIR PREY IN TYW AS INDICATORS OF MANAGEMENT SUCCESS AND (4) TRAIN UNDERGRADUATE WILDLIFE STUDENTS FROM KASETSART UNIVERSITY ON SMART PATROL AND WILDLIFE MONITORING TECHNIQUES.</narrative>
  </description>
